{
  "info": {
    "name": "Autotask -> aBILLity Company Name Sync",
    "description": "Registers the Autotask webhook that drives the company name sync, as an alternative to running autotask-abillity-sync.ps1.\n\nSETUP\n  Open the collection's Variables tab and fill in userName, apiIntegrationCode, secret, webhookUrl, deactivationUrl, notificationEmail, and your two UDF labels.\n  Leave baseUrl and everything ending in Id blank - the requests fill those in as they run.\n\nORDER\n  Run requests 0 to 7 in order, top to bottom. Each one stores what the next needs.\n  Request 0 sends no credentials and is always safe to run.\n  Request 2 creates the webhook - run it only once.\n\nWATCH THE CONSOLE\n  Open Postman's console (View > Show Postman Console) before running. The test scripts log what they captured, and request 5 lists every Company UDF label Autotask reports if yours do not match.\n\nA NOTE ON LOCKOUTS\n  A 401 means either wrong credentials or a locked account - they are indistinguishable. Repeated failures lock the account, so do not retry request 1 over and over. Fix the values, or get the account unlocked, then try once.\n\nTESTING THE SYNC\n  The 'Test the sync' folder renames a company in Autotask to fire the webhook end to end. T2 is read-only and checks the two UDFs are set. T3 and T4 write to live data in Autotask and, through the sync, in aBILLity.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0. Get zone information (no credentials sent)",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "https://webservices2.autotask.net/atservicesrest/V1.0/zoneInformation?user={{userName}}"
        },
        "description": "Finds which Autotask server your account lives on and stores it as {{baseUrl}}.\n\nThis request sends NO credentials, so it cannot lock anything. Run it first.\n\nIf it does not return a url, the username is not a recognised Autotask API user."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "const json = pm.response.json();",
              "",
              "pm.test('Zone lookup returned a url', function () {",
              "    pm.expect(json.url, 'no url in response').to.be.a('string');",
              "});",
              "",
              "if (json.url) {",
              "    const base = json.url.replace(/\\/+$/, '');",
              "    pm.collectionVariables.set('baseUrl', base);",
              "    console.log('baseUrl set to: ' + base);",
              "    console.log('It should end in /ATServicesRest - if it does not, stop and check.');",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "1. Test credentials",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "ApiIntegrationcode",
            "value": "{{apiIntegrationCode}}"
          },
          {
            "key": "UserName",
            "value": "{{userName}}"
          },
          {
            "key": "Secret",
            "value": "{{secret}}"
          },
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/V1.0/Companies/entityInformation"
        },
        "description": "One authenticated request, to confirm the credentials before creating anything.\n\n200 = credentials good.\n401 = rejected (wrong values, OR the account is locked - both look the same).\n403 = credentials valid but this API user lacks permission.\n\nDo not hammer this. Each failure counts toward a lockout."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
              "    console.log('Credentials accepted.');",
              "} else if (pm.response.code === 401) {",
              "    console.log('401 - credentials rejected, OR the account is locked.');",
              "    console.log('A locked account looks identical to a wrong password here.');",
              "    console.log('Do not retry repeatedly - each attempt counts toward a lockout.');",
              "} else if (pm.response.code === 403) {",
              "    console.log('403 - credentials are VALID but lack permission (Security Level).');",
              "} else {",
              "    console.log('Unexpected status ' + pm.response.code);",
              "}",
              "",
              "pm.test('Credentials accepted (200)', function () {",
              "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2. Create the webhook",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "ApiIntegrationcode",
            "value": "{{apiIntegrationCode}}"
          },
          {
            "key": "UserName",
            "value": "{{userName}}"
          },
          {
            "key": "Secret",
            "value": "{{secret}}"
          },
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/V1.0/CompanyWebhooks"
        },
        "description": "Creates the webhook and stores its id as {{webhookId}}.\n\nOnly run this ONCE. Running it again creates a duplicate webhook - use 'List webhooks' and 'Delete webhook' at the bottom to tidy up.",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"IsActive\": true,\n  \"DeactivationUrl\": \"{{deactivationUrl}}\",\n  \"IsSubscribedToUpdateEvents\": true,\n  \"Name\": \"Company Name -> aBILLity Sync\",\n  \"SecretKey\": \"{{$guid}}\",\n  \"SendThresholdExceededNotification\": true,\n  \"WebhookUrl\": \"{{webhookUrl}}\",\n  \"NotificationEmailAddress\": \"{{notificationEmail}}\"\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "const json = pm.response.json();",
              "",
              "pm.test('Webhook created', function () {",
              "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
              "    pm.expect(json.itemId, 'no itemId returned').to.be.ok;",
              "});",
              "",
              "if (json.itemId) {",
              "    pm.collectionVariables.set('webhookId', json.itemId);",
              "    console.log('webhookId set to: ' + json.itemId);",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "3. Find the CompanyName fieldID",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "ApiIntegrationcode",
            "value": "{{apiIntegrationCode}}"
          },
          {
            "key": "UserName",
            "value": "{{userName}}"
          },
          {
            "key": "Secret",
            "value": "{{secret}}"
          },
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/V1.0/CompanyWebhookFields/entityInformation/fields"
        },
        "description": "Looks up the numeric id Autotask uses for the CompanyName field, and stores it as {{companyNameFieldId}}."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "const fields = (pm.response.json().fields) || [];",
              "const fieldIdField = fields.find(f => f.name === 'fieldID');",
              "const values = (fieldIdField && fieldIdField.picklistValues) || [];",
              "const match = values.find(v => v.label === 'CompanyName');",
              "",
              "pm.test('CompanyName field found', function () {",
              "    pm.expect(match, 'no picklist value labelled CompanyName').to.be.ok;",
              "});",
              "",
              "if (match) {",
              "    pm.collectionVariables.set('companyNameFieldId', match.value);",
              "    console.log('companyNameFieldId set to: ' + match.value);",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "4. Register CompanyName as the trigger field",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "ApiIntegrationcode",
            "value": "{{apiIntegrationCode}}"
          },
          {
            "key": "UserName",
            "value": "{{userName}}"
          },
          {
            "key": "Secret",
            "value": "{{secret}}"
          },
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/V1.0/CompanyWebhooks/{{webhookId}}/Fields"
        },
        "description": "Makes a change to the company name the thing that fires the webhook.",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"FieldID\": \"{{companyNameFieldId}}\",\n  \"IsSubscribedField\": true,\n  \"IsDisplayAlwaysField\": true,\n  \"WebhookID\": \"{{webhookId}}\"\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Trigger field registered', function () {",
              "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "5. Find both UDF field IDs",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "ApiIntegrationcode",
            "value": "{{apiIntegrationCode}}"
          },
          {
            "key": "UserName",
            "value": "{{userName}}"
          },
          {
            "key": "Secret",
            "value": "{{secret}}"
          },
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/V1.0/CompanyWebhookUdfFields/entityInformation/fields"
        },
        "description": "Finds the numeric ids for your two Company UDFs, matching on the labels in {{abillityIdUdfLabel}} and {{syncFlagUdfLabel}}.\n\nIf either is not found, the console lists every Company UDF label Autotask reports - copy the exact spelling from there into the collection variables."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "const fields = (pm.response.json().fields) || [];",
              "const udfField = fields.find(f => f.name === 'udfFieldID');",
              "const values = (udfField && udfField.picklistValues) || [];",
              "",
              "const idLabel = pm.collectionVariables.get('abillityIdUdfLabel');",
              "const flagLabel = pm.collectionVariables.get('syncFlagUdfLabel');",
              "",
              "const idMatch = values.find(v => v.label === idLabel);",
              "const flagMatch = values.find(v => v.label === flagLabel);",
              "",
              "if (!idMatch || !flagMatch) {",
              "    console.log('--- Company UDF labels Autotask actually reports ---');",
              "    values.map(v => v.label).sort().forEach(l => console.log('  ' + JSON.stringify(l)));",
              "    console.log('---------------------------------------------------');",
              "    console.log('Copy the exact spelling into the collection variables.');",
              "}",
              "",
              "pm.test('aBILLity ID UDF found: ' + idLabel, function () {",
              "    pm.expect(idMatch, 'no UDF labelled ' + JSON.stringify(idLabel)).to.be.ok;",
              "});",
              "",
              "pm.test('Sync flag UDF found: ' + flagLabel, function () {",
              "    pm.expect(flagMatch, 'no UDF labelled ' + JSON.stringify(flagLabel)).to.be.ok;",
              "});",
              "",
              "if (idMatch) {",
              "    pm.collectionVariables.set('abillityIdUdfFieldId', idMatch.value);",
              "    console.log('abillityIdUdfFieldId set to: ' + idMatch.value);",
              "}",
              "if (flagMatch) {",
              "    pm.collectionVariables.set('syncFlagUdfFieldId', flagMatch.value);",
              "    console.log('syncFlagUdfFieldId set to: ' + flagMatch.value);",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "6. Register UDF: {{abillityIdUdfLabel}}",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "ApiIntegrationcode",
            "value": "{{apiIntegrationCode}}"
          },
          {
            "key": "UserName",
            "value": "{{userName}}"
          },
          {
            "key": "Secret",
            "value": "{{secret}}"
          },
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/V1.0/CompanyWebhooks/{{webhookId}}/UdfFields"
        },
        "description": "Adds this UDF to the webhook payload as a display-always field. It does not trigger the webhook - it just rides along so the receiver can read it.",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"UdfFieldID\": \"{{abillityIdUdfFieldId}}\",\n  \"IsSubscribedField\": false,\n  \"IsDisplayAlwaysField\": true,\n  \"WebhookID\": \"{{webhookId}}\"\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('UDF registered', function () {",
              "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "7. Register UDF: {{syncFlagUdfLabel}}",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "ApiIntegrationcode",
            "value": "{{apiIntegrationCode}}"
          },
          {
            "key": "UserName",
            "value": "{{userName}}"
          },
          {
            "key": "Secret",
            "value": "{{secret}}"
          },
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/V1.0/CompanyWebhooks/{{webhookId}}/UdfFields"
        },
        "description": "Adds this UDF to the webhook payload as a display-always field. It does not trigger the webhook - it just rides along so the receiver can read it.",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"UdfFieldID\": \"{{syncFlagUdfFieldId}}\",\n  \"IsSubscribedField\": false,\n  \"IsDisplayAlwaysField\": true,\n  \"WebhookID\": \"{{webhookId}}\"\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('UDF registered', function () {",
              "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Test the sync (WRITES LIVE DATA)",
      "description": "End-to-end test: rename a company in Autotask and watch it reach aBILLity.\n\nT1 finds a company, T2 checks its two UDFs are set (read-only, and the most useful one - a company that is not flagged will be skipped by design), T3 renames it and fires the sync, T4 puts the name back.\n\nT3 and T4 write to Autotask AND, through the sync, to aBILLity.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "T1. Find a company by name",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "ApiIntegrationcode",
                "value": "{{apiIntegrationCode}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "UserName",
                "value": "{{userName}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Secret",
                "value": "{{secret}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/V1.0/Companies/query?search={\"filter\":[{\"op\":\"contains\",\"field\":\"companyName\",\"value\":\"{{testCompanySearch}}\"}]}"
            },
            "description": "Finds companies whose name contains {{testCompanySearch}}, so you can pick one to test with and copy its id into {{testCompanyId}}.\n\nRead-only."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const items = (pm.response.json().items) || [];",
                  "console.log(items.length + ' match(es):');",
                  "items.slice(0, 25).forEach(c => console.log('  id ' + c.id + '  ' + c.companyName));",
                  "if (items.length === 1) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('testCompanyId', items[0].id);",
                  "    console.log('One match - testCompanyId set to ' + items[0].id);",
                  "}",
                  "pm.test('Search returned something', function () { pm.expect(items.length).to.be.above(0); });"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "T2. Check the company is set up (read-only)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "ApiIntegrationcode",
                "value": "{{apiIntegrationCode}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "UserName",
                "value": "{{userName}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Secret",
                "value": "{{secret}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/V1.0/Companies/{{testCompanyId}}"
            },
            "description": "Shows the company's current name and, crucially, the values of your two UDFs.\n\nRun this BEFORE renaming. If the sync flag is not yes or the aBILLity id is blank, the Worker will correctly skip the rename and you will think the sync is broken when it is doing exactly what it should.\n\nRead-only. Captures the current name into {{originalCompanyName}} so T4 can restore it."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "const c = j.item || (j.items && j.items[0]) || j;",
                  "",
                  "const idLabel = pm.collectionVariables.get('abillityIdUdfLabel');",
                  "const flagLabel = pm.collectionVariables.get('syncFlagUdfLabel');",
                  "const udfs = c.userDefinedFields || [];",
                  "const find = (label) => (udfs.find(u => u.name === label) || {}).value;",
                  "",
                  "console.log('--- company ' + c.id + ' ---');",
                  "console.log('name : ' + c.companyName);",
                  "console.log(JSON.stringify(flagLabel) + ' = ' + JSON.stringify(find(flagLabel)));",
                  "console.log(JSON.stringify(idLabel) + ' = ' + JSON.stringify(find(idLabel)));",
                  "",
                  "if (udfs.length) {",
                  "    console.log('all UDFs on this company:');",
                  "    udfs.forEach(u => console.log('  ' + JSON.stringify(u.name) + ' = ' + JSON.stringify(u.value)));",
                  "}",
                  "",
                  "if (c.companyName) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('originalCompanyName', c.companyName);",
                  "    console.log('Original name stored - T4 restores it.');",
                  "}",
                  "",
                  "const flag = String(find(flagLabel) || '').trim().toLowerCase();",
                  "const syncOn = ['yes','y','true','1','on','checked'].indexOf(flag) !== -1;",
                  "const hasId = !!find(idLabel);",
                  "",
                  "if (!syncOn) { console.log('WARNING: sync flag is not yes - the Worker will skip this company.'); }",
                  "if (!hasId)  { console.log('WARNING: no aBILLity id - the Worker will skip this company.'); }",
                  "if (syncOn && hasId) { console.log('Set up correctly - renaming this company should sync.'); }",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Company found', function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
                  "pm.test('Flagged for sync', function () { pm.expect(syncOn, 'sync flag is not yes').to.be.true; });",
                  "pm.test('Has an aBILLity id', function () { pm.expect(hasId, 'aBILLity id is blank').to.be.true; });"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "T3. Rename the company (FIRES THE SYNC)",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "ApiIntegrationcode",
                "value": "{{apiIntegrationCode}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "UserName",
                "value": "{{userName}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Secret",
                "value": "{{secret}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/V1.0/Companies"
            },
            "description": "Renames the company in Autotask, which is what fires the webhook.\n\n*** THIS WRITES TO LIVE DATA IN TWO SYSTEMS. *** The rename lands in Autotask, and if the sync works it renames the matching company in aBILLity too.\n\nRun T2 first so the original name is captured, then T4 to put it back - T4 fires the sync again and restores the aBILLity name as well.\n\nStart the Worker's log stream before running this.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"id\": \"{{testCompanyId}}\",\n  \"companyName\": \"{{testCompanyName}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Rename accepted', function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
                  "",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "    console.log('Renamed to ' + JSON.stringify(pm.collectionVariables.get('testCompanyName')));",
                  "    console.log('Now watch the Worker log. Within a minute or so expect:');",
                  "    console.log('  Request: POST /api/CompanyNameSync');",
                  "    console.log('  Synced company <abillity id> -> ...');",
                  "    console.log('Nothing at all means Autotask did not call the Worker.');",
                  "    console.log('Then run T4 to restore ' + JSON.stringify(pm.collectionVariables.get('originalCompanyName')));",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "T4. Restore the original name",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "ApiIntegrationcode",
                "value": "{{apiIntegrationCode}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "UserName",
                "value": "{{userName}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Secret",
                "value": "{{secret}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/V1.0/Companies"
            },
            "description": "Puts the Autotask name back to whatever T2 captured, which fires the sync again and restores the aBILLity name too.\n\nIf {{originalCompanyName}} is empty, T2 did not capture it - set the name by hand rather than running this.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"id\": \"{{testCompanyId}}\",\n  \"companyName\": \"{{originalCompanyName}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const original = pm.collectionVariables.get('originalCompanyName');",
                  "if (!original) {",
                  "    console.log('WARNING: {{originalCompanyName}} is empty - this just sent a blank name.');",
                  "    console.log('Fix the company name by hand in Autotask.');",
                  "}",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "    console.log('Restored to ' + JSON.stringify(original));",
                  "} else {",
                  "    console.log('RESTORE FAILED (' + pm.response.code + '). The company is still renamed.');",
                  "}",
                  "pm.test('Restored', function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Utilities",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "List webhooks",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "ApiIntegrationcode",
                "value": "{{apiIntegrationCode}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "UserName",
                "value": "{{userName}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Secret",
                "value": "{{secret}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/V1.0/CompanyWebhooks/query?search={\"filter\":[{\"op\":\"gte\",\"field\":\"id\",\"value\":0}]}"
            },
            "description": "Shows every Company webhook on the account. Use it to confirm what was created, or to find the id of a duplicate you want to remove."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const items = (pm.response.json().items) || [];",
                  "console.log(items.length + ' webhook(s):');",
                  "items.forEach(w => console.log('  id ' + w.id + '  ' + w.name + '  active=' + w.isActive));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Get webhook {{webhookId}}",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "ApiIntegrationcode",
                "value": "{{apiIntegrationCode}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "UserName",
                "value": "{{userName}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Secret",
                "value": "{{secret}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/V1.0/CompanyWebhooks/{{webhookId}}"
            },
            "description": "Shows the webhook's current settings. Run it before and after an update to confirm the change landed."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "const w = j.item || (j.items && j.items[0]) || j;",
                  "",
                  "console.log('--- webhook ' + w.id + ' ---');",
                  "console.log('name           : ' + w.name);",
                  "console.log('isActive       : ' + w.isActive);",
                  "console.log('webhookUrl     : ' + w.webhookUrl);",
                  "console.log('deactivationUrl: ' + w.deactivationUrl);",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Webhook found', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "    pm.expect(w, 'no webhook in response').to.be.ok;",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "if (w.isActive === false) {",
                  "    console.log('NOTE: this webhook is INACTIVE. Autotask deactivates webhooks whose');",
                  "    console.log('endpoint keeps failing. Add \"IsActive\": true to the update body to');",
                  "    console.log('switch it back on once the URL is correct.');",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Update webhook URLs",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "ApiIntegrationcode",
                "value": "{{apiIntegrationCode}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "UserName",
                "value": "{{userName}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Secret",
                "value": "{{secret}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/V1.0/CompanyWebhooks"
            },
            "description": "Changes an existing webhook's two URLs without deleting and recreating it, so the trigger field and UDF registrations from requests 4, 6 and 7 are kept.\n\nSet the webhookUrl and deactivationUrl collection variables to the new values first, and make sure webhookId is the webhook you mean to change - 'List webhooks' shows them all.\n\nIf the webhook has been deactivated (Autotask switches off webhooks whose endpoint keeps failing), add \"IsActive\": true to the body to turn it back on.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"id\": \"{{webhookId}}\",\n  \"WebhookUrl\": \"{{webhookUrl}}\",\n  \"DeactivationUrl\": \"{{deactivationUrl}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Webhook updated', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "    console.log('Updated webhook ' + pm.collectionVariables.get('webhookId'));",
                  "    console.log('  webhookUrl      -> ' + pm.collectionVariables.get('webhookUrl'));",
                  "    console.log('  deactivationUrl -> ' + pm.collectionVariables.get('deactivationUrl'));",
                  "    console.log('Run \"Get webhook\" to confirm.');",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Delete webhook {{webhookId}}",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "ApiIntegrationcode",
                "value": "{{apiIntegrationCode}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "UserName",
                "value": "{{userName}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Secret",
                "value": "{{secret}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/V1.0/CompanyWebhooks/{{webhookId}}"
            },
            "description": "Deletes the webhook currently in {{webhookId}}. Use this to clean up a duplicate or start over.\n\nSet {{webhookId}} by hand first if you want to delete a different one."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Webhook deleted', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
